    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nI would like to\r\n\r\n- disable function call `\"f\"` surround. Tried setting `custom_surroundings = { f = false }` (as in mini.ai), but it throws an error: `Error executing lua vim/shared.lua:0: after the second argument: expected table, got boolean`\r\n- remap original function call to `\"C\"`, but use the treesitter gen_spec for all operations except `sa`, where it fails. In such case I would like to use function call as provided by surround.mini.\r\n\r\nIs such fine-grained control possible? Thanks!",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hi,</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I would like to</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>disable function call <code class=\"notranslate\">\"f\"</code> surround. Tried setting <code class=\"notranslate\">custom_surroundings = { f = false }</code> (as in mini.ai), but it throws an error: <code class=\"notranslate\">Error executing lua vim/shared.lua:0: after the second argument: expected table, got boolean</code></li>\n<li>remap original function call to <code class=\"notranslate\">\"C\"</code>, but use the treesitter gen_spec for all operations except <code class=\"notranslate\">sa</code>, where it fails. In such case I would like to use function call as provided by surround.mini.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is such fine-grained control possible? Thanks!</p>",
    "bodyText": "Hi,\nI would like to\n\ndisable function call \"f\" surround. Tried setting custom_surroundings = { f = false } (as in mini.ai), but it throws an error: Error executing lua vim/shared.lua:0: after the second argument: expected table, got boolean\nremap original function call to \"C\", but use the treesitter gen_spec for all operations except sa, where it fails. In such case I would like to use function call as provided by surround.mini.\n\nIs such fine-grained control possible? Thanks!",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
