                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "`srC` does work as expected with this config. For example, `srC)` finds function call based on `@call.outer` and `@call.inner` tree-sitter queries and replaces it with parenthesis.\r\n\r\nDo you have necessary queries set up [as described in help page](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/doc/mini-surround.txt#L752-L770)? Usually it means just installing 'nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects' (without needing to \"activate\" it).",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">srC</code> does work as expected with this config. For example, <code class=\"notranslate\">srC)</code> finds function call based on <code class=\"notranslate\">@call.outer</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">@call.inner</code> tree-sitter queries and replaces it with parenthesis.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Do you have necessary queries set up <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/doc/mini-surround.txt#L752-L770\">as described in help page</a>? Usually it means just installing 'nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects' (without needing to \"activate\" it).</p>",
                    "bodyText": "srC does work as expected with this config. For example, srC) finds function call based on @call.outer and @call.inner tree-sitter queries and replaces it with parenthesis.\nDo you have necessary queries set up as described in help page? Usually it means just installing 'nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects' (without needing to \"activate\" it).",
