                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "\"Replace\" operator requires two identifiers: first to find the one to be replaced, second to define with which it should be replaced (as [shown in examples](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a3f274633a57c713160baf51724ecfc051117877/doc/mini-surround.txt#L77)). So to rename a function call, it is `srCC` - replace function call with another function call (which will show prompt for function name). This is by design to allow more flexible \"replace\" operator (instead of \"rename\").",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">\"Replace\" operator requires two identifiers: first to find the one to be replaced, second to define with which it should be replaced (as <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a3f274633a57c713160baf51724ecfc051117877/doc/mini-surround.txt#L77\">shown in examples</a>). So to rename a function call, it is <code class=\"notranslate\">srCC</code> - replace function call with another function call (which will show prompt for function name). This is by design to allow more flexible \"replace\" operator (instead of \"rename\").</p>",
                    "bodyText": "\"Replace\" operator requires two identifiers: first to find the one to be replaced, second to define with which it should be replaced (as shown in examples). So to rename a function call, it is srCC - replace function call with another function call (which will show prompt for function name). This is by design to allow more flexible \"replace\" operator (instead of \"rename\").",
